    <bpmn:process id="W_W3094" name="W3094. Dark Store Go-Live, Pilot &amp; Ramp-Up" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Site commissioned and staff trained
Frequency: Per new site
Volume: Phased: pilot store catchment → metro → multi-metro
Owner: Dark Store Operations Manager
Participants: Dark Store Ops Mgr, GM, Digital Commerce Inc., IT, Quality, CS, Marketing
Source: workflow W3094 — Dark Store Go-Live, Pilot &amp; Ramp-Up</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3094_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3094_Lane1" name="Ecommerce Ops Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3094_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3094_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3094_Lane2" name="Dark Store Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3094_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3094_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3094_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3094_Start4" name="Site commissioned and staff trained">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3094_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3094_Task5" name="Ecommerce/ORM team (links to VS-60) begins routing a controlled % of eligible…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Ecommerce/ORM team (links to VS-60) begins routing a controlled % of eligible orders to the new dark store (e.g., 5% → 25% → 50% → 100% over 4–6 weeks), geofenced to the catchment area, with daily SLA and accuracy review
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops Lead
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 4–6 weeks ramp</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3094_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3094_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3094_Task6" name="Dark Store Ops Mgr runs daily war-room during hyper-care: review order cycle…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Dark Store Ops Mgr runs daily war-room during hyper-care: review order cycle time, pick accuracy, pack quality, dispatch-on-time, rider wait time, exceptions; resolve systemic issues with IT/Vendor
Responsible (R): Dark Store Operations Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Daily during ramp</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3094_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3094_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3094_Task7" name="At end of ramp: ops review against business case (cost-per-order, orders/hour…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: At end of ramp: ops review against business case (cost-per-order, orders/hour, SLA); decide steady-state ownership transfer, hand back to standard daily ops (PA-93.2), and publish post-implementation report
Responsible (R): Dark Store Operations Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 week wrap-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3094_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3094_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3094_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3094_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3094_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-508 (ensure controlled execution — Dark Store Site Strategy, Design &amp; Network Planning (PA-93.1).) | - operational: capped ramp % and daily KPI gates
Owner: Dark Store Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
